<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Icon for the "New mask" launcher shortcut (res/xml/shortcuts.xml).

    A launcher shortcut icon is NOT tinted by anyone: the launcher draws the
    drawable as it is. A bare white silhouette therefore disappeared — Launcher3
    wraps a non-adaptive icon in a white circle before drawing it, so white ink
    on a white disc is exactly the empty circle the shortcut menu showed.

    An adaptive icon fixes that at the root instead of guessing the backdrop:
    it brings its own opaque cream background, so the mask stays legible under a
    light or a dark shortcut popup, and the launcher masks it into whatever shape
    it uses for app icons rather than inventing a fallback.

    Deliberately a separate resource from ic_quick_mask.xml — that one is the
    monochrome glyph for surfaces that tint (QS tile, notifications), this one is
    a full-colour icon for a surface that does not. One file cannot be both.
-->
<adaptive-icon xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <background android:drawable="@drawable/ic_launcher_background" />
    <foreground android:drawable="@drawable/ic_shortcut_quick_mask_foreground" />
</adaptive-icon>
